# Everything the image build does not read. Two entries here are load-bearing
# rather than merely tidy.
#
# .git: keeping it out means the history does not land in a layer, and the
# context hash stops changing on every commit. The cost is that the build cannot
# resolve its own commit, which is what --build-arg PEREDUR_GIT_COMMIT supplies.
#
# build*/: a host build tree would overwrite the third_party the tools stage
# copied in, and with it the done-stamps that let the build skip Spot.
.git
.gitignore
.githooks
build
build-*

.direnv
.envrc
.cache
.ruff_cache
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.profraw

# Campaign archives, prose and crash reports: nothing here is compiled, and
# every one of them would otherwise invalidate the COPY layer above the build
# whenever it changed. cmake/docs.cmake reads docs/ only when Doxygen, Sphinx
# and KaTeX are all present, and the builder stage has none of them.
experiments
crashes
outputs
docs
README.md
CLAUDE.md
EXPERIMENTS.md
PLAN.md
.github

Dockerfile
.dockerignore
